{title: Rushing Violent Wind}
{subtitle: Acts 2:1–4}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [Bb]day of Pentecost had finally come
[Eb]They were all together in [Bb]one place
Waiting for the promise to be fulfilled
In the [Eb]quiet of that gath[Bb]ered [Gm]space
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Suddenly a sound [Dm]came from the sky
Like a [Eb]rushing, violent [Bb]wind
It [Gm]filled the whole house where they [Dm]sat
And [Eb]the air began to [F]spin
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Tongues as of fire ap[Gm]peared and divided
[Eb]Coming to rest [F]on [Bb]each of them
Filled with the Holy [Gm]Spirit completely
[Eb]Speaking in [F]other tongues a[Bb]gain [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Devout Jews from every nation
[Eb]Living in Jerusa[Bb]lem now
When the sound was heard [Gm]by the crowd
[Eb]They gathered in a be[Bb]wildered hour
[Gm]Each one heard them [Dm]speaking clearly
[Eb]In his own lan[F]guage, strange and [Bb]true
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Tongues as of fire ap[Gm]peared and divided
[Eb]Coming to rest [F]on [Bb]each of them
Filled with the Holy [Gm]Spirit completely
[Eb]Speaking in [F]other tongues a[Bb]gain [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]They were astounded [Gm]and amazed
Say[Eb]ing look at these spea[Bb]kers here
Are not all [Gm]these Galileans
Who [Eb]stand before us with such [Bb]fear
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
As the Spirit gave them utterance
The world heard the [F]word in its [Bb]own tongue
{end_of_verse}
